# Raw Inspect logs: they contain the environments' secrets (passwords, keys) and can't be redacted.
# The readable, redacted records in 3-experiments/*/runs/ are the shareable copies. Never push these.
*.eval

# Generated
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.building.html

# Editor and OneDrive temporary files
~$*
*.tmp
.DS_Store

# The Nov 1 pilot transcripts come from environments whose credentials the record redaction doesn't cover,
# so they stay out of the repository (they are not needed to run anything).
3-experiments/linuxarena-pilot/transcripts/

# Raw data stays in WSL under /root/power-v0/ (3-experiments/linuxarena-power-v0/findings/data-map.md): snapshots,
# database and bucket dumps, and saved machine states (files.tar, pg.tar, s3/, *.nul) hold the environment's secrets.
# These catch them, and other secrets and large binaries, if they're ever copied in by mistake.
# runs/ stays tracked: its records are redacted and meant to be committed.
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.nul
*.dump
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.pem
*.key
.env
*.env
ct.env*
**/data/states/
**/data/rollback/
**/data/evals/
**/data/runs/
snapshot.txt
db_s3.txt
